body:
So recently I've joined good old tinder looking for love and have been chatting to a few guys. Theres one guy I'm talking to who seems cool but from his profile I have no idea how tall he is, so I just ask him. He gets all weird and cagey and lets me know he's 5'9. I sent back something like 'ah rip I'm 6ft' and he replies back 'so?'. I then kinda told him I just didn't really want to date anyone shorter than me and he launched into how I'm a horrible shallow person and I'm like every other girl wanting a guy that is at least 6ft. Not going to lie his rant kinda shook me a bit. 

&amp;#x200B;

Like maybe it is shallow but god damn I just want to feel like a female for once and feel small and protected. I feel like bloody Sasquatch with all my friends who are like 5'2. 

&amp;#x200B;

(Really curious to see what the response to this is)
